The token payload is decoded in **`src/auth/service.ts`**, in the **`decodeJwt`** function (lines 9–13):

```ts
export function decodeJwt(token: string): Record<string, unknown> {
  const [, payload] = token.split('.');
  const json = atob(payload.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/'));
  return JSON.parse(json);
}
```

It splits the JWT on `.`, converts the base64url payload segment to standard base64 (`-`→`+`, `_`→`/`), and runs it through `atob` before `JSON.parse`. Note it's currently unused elsewhere in `src/` (no call sites found), and it doesn't re-pad the base64url string with `=` before calling `atob` — base64url payloads aren't always a multiple of 4 characters, so `atob` can throw or return truncated/garbled output depending on the payload length, which would match the "garbled profile data" symptom.

I haven't made any edits, per your request — let me know if you'd like me to fix the padding issue.
